{
  "id": "80833",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Weak Acid–Strong Base Titrations: Overview",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The titration of a weak acid with a strong base (or a weak base with a strong acid) is somewhat more complicated than a strong acid–strong base titration, but it follows the same general principles. When a weak acid is titrated with a strong base, the strong acid and strong base react completely until one of the species is used up, and the species remaining after reaction then reach equilibrium. The pH at any given point in the titration depends on the relative amounts of both species at that point. We need to determine the moles of the major species after reaction, then do equilibrium calculations involving either "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": " or "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": ". To understand the pH calculations, it can be useful to consider the titration as having four phases."
              }
            ],
            "id": "6c1cg430i7lcmv2",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "4dnckdyeefmeamm",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "8ghhc3rtgvhtyxp",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/A3/A31F9808B584CB71B1FEA56DD0BCDE4E/green_line.png",
            "type": "img"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "fyf30jyyhl4jw5q",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "p445wuc4f0pxpgh",
            "items": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "329933063",
                    "type": "p"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": " As previously discussed, a weak acid (HA) will partially dissociate to form H"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "3"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "O"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "+"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " and A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " according to the reaction:"
                              },
                              {
                                "children": [
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "type": "text"
                                  }
                                ],
                                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                                "src": "\\mathrm{HA}(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\:{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm A^-(aq)",
                                "subtype": "latex",
                                "type": "formula_inline"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "An ICE table can be used to determine the equilibrium concentrations. Then the "
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "K"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "a"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " expression can be used to determine [H"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "3"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "O"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "+"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "]"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "eq"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ", which can be used to calculate pH.  "
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "3630869461",
                            "type": "p"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "li"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": " "
                              },
                              {
                                "strong": true,
                                "text": "Before the Equivalence Point"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "When a strong base (OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ") is added to the weak acid solution, the OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " reacts with HA to produce additional A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ", thereby decreasing the amount of HA and increasing the amount of A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ":"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": ""
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "3651574523",
                            "src": "\\mathrm{HA}(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm A^-(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "We first determine [HA] and [A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "] after the reaction is complete. We then use these concentrations, the acid-ionization reaction, and the "
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "K"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "a"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " expression to determine [H"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "3"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "O"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "+"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "] and pH:"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": ""
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "1317235645",
                            "src": "\\mathrm{HA}(aq)\\;+\\:{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+(aq)\\:+\\:\\mathrm A^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm a}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack{\\mathrm H}_3\\mathrm O^+\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm A^-\\rbrack}{\\lbrack\\mathrm{HA}\\rbrack}",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "li"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "strong": true,
                                "text": "At the Equivalence Point"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "At the equivalence point of a weak acid–strong base titration, the initial amount of weak acid and the amount of added strong base are both completely consumed, and the reaction produces the conjugate base of the weak acid (A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ")."
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": ""
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "3567505177",
                            "src": "\\mathrm{HA}(aq)\\;+\\;\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\longrightarrow\\;\\;\\mathrm A^-(aq)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "The A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " that is produced then reacts with H"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "2"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "O to form the weak acid and OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ", thus affecting the pH of the solution. Unlike the strong acid–strong base titration, at the equivalence point of a weak acid–strong base titration, solution is not neutral and the pH will "
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "not"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " be 7—the solution is basic and the pH will be greater than 7."
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "We first determine [A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "] after the reaction is complete. We then use this concentration, the base-ionization reaction for A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ", and the "
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "K"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "b"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " expression to determine [OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "] and pH:"
                              }
                            ],
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": ""
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "3152465279",
                            "src": "\\mathrm A^-(aq)\\;+\\:{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{HA}(aq)\\:+\\:\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm b}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm{HA}\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^-\\rbrack}{\\lbrack\\mathrm A^-\\rbrack}",
                            "subtype": "latex",
                            "type": "formula"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "li"
                      },
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "strong": true,
                                "text": "After the Equivalence Point"
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "1014086941",
                            "type": "p"
                          },
                          {
                            "children": [
                              {
                                "text": "In this region, all of the moles of weak acid, HA, have been converted into its conjugate base, A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ", and additional moles of reactant OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " have been added to the solution. The solution is basic, and the pH is determined using the concentrations of A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " and OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " after reaction, the base-ionization reaction for A"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": ", and the "
                              },
                              {
                                "em": true,
                                "text": "K"
                              },
                              {
                                "sub": true,
                                "text": "b"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " expression:  "
                              },
                              {
                                "children": [
                                  {
                                    "text": " ",
                                    "type": "text"
                                  }
                                ],
                                "legacyBlockRendered": true,
                                "src": "\\mathrm A^-(aq)\\;+\\:{\\mathrm H}_2\\mathrm O(l)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;\\mathrm{HA}(aq)\\: +\\:\\mathrm{OH}^-(aq)\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;\\;K_{\\mathrm b}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\lbrack\\mathrm{HA}\\rbrack\\lbrack\\mathrm{OH}^- \\rbrack}{\\lbrack\\mathrm A^-\\rbrack}",
                                "subtype": "latex",
                                "type": "formula_inline"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "We find that the pH of the solution is determined almost completely by the OH"
                              },
                              {
                                "sup": true,
                                "text": "−"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": " added past the equivalence point."
                              }
                            ],
                            "id": "3747123521",
                            "type": "p"
                          }
                        ],
                        "type": "li"
                      }
                    ],
                    "style": "decimal",
                    "type": "ol"
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": ""
                      }
